SSIS (ETL)   +   SSRS (Reporting)  —  used by all LOBs" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FBEADA;strokeColor=#D79B00;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#222222;arcSize=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="870.0" y="1020" width="440" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="n99" value="―――  Live application traffic (request / response)          - - -  Scheduled ETL / shared-service data flow
API Nodes = servers running the API tier      UI Nodes = servers running the UI tier      CLS = Cluster      BGP = On-Prem load-balancing/routing layer
Every LOB follows the same pattern: Load Balancer → App+UI Cluster → App DB + ETL DB, with SSIS/SSRS as shared services across all LOBs.
Note: &#x27;API Nodes / UI Nodes&#x27; values are read from the source diagram as (API + UI) in that order — please confirm if reversed. JSM sizing is pending." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FAFAFA;strokeColor=#DDDDDD;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#555555;arcSize=8;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1120" width="2100" height="95" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
